  "items": [
    {
      "original_text": "SC1: ticket link task-A task-B blocks|depends_on where task-A and task-B share the same parent story \u2192 link written as-is (intra-story dependency, allowed).",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system rule for how ticket linking behaves when tasks share a parent story, phrased as ongoing permitted behavior"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "SC2: ticket link story-X story-Y blocks|depends_on where story-X and story-Y share the same parent epic \u2192 link written as-is (intra-epic story dependency, allowed).",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system behavior where the linking mechanism supports and preserves intra-epic story dependencies"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "SC3: ticket link task-A task-B blocks|depends_on where task-A is under story-X (epic-P) and task-B is under story-Y (epic-P, same epic) \u2192 promoted to story-X \u2192 story-Y; redirect notice printed to stderr.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "transitional",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a one-time promotion/reorganization of tasks and a notice print action, not an ongoing system property"
      },
      "user_decision": "accept",
      "post_migration_section": "CC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "SC4: ticket link story-X story-Y blocks|depends_on where story-X and story-Y are under different epics \u2192 promoted to epic-P \u2192 epic-Q; redirect notice to stderr.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "transitional",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a one-time restructuring/promotion action with a specific redirection task, not an ongoing system property"
      },
      "user_decision": "accept",
      "post_migration_section": "CC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "SC5: ticket link task-A task-B blocks|depends_on where the tasks are under different epics \u2192 promoted to epic-P \u2192 epic-Q; redirect notice to stderr.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "transitional",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a one-time organizational action of promoting tasks to a new epic and adding a redirect notice, not an ongoing system property"
      },
      "user_decision": "accept",
      "post_migration_section": "CC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "SC6: ticket link <any-ticket> <epic-B> blocks|depends_on where the ticket's root epic differs from epic-B \u2192 promoted to source-root-epic \u2192 epic-B; redirect notice to stderr.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system behavior for handling cross-epic ticket relationships and redirecting notices, not a one-time migration task"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "SC7: ticket link story-A epic-P blocks|depends_on (or the reverse) where epic-P is story-A's direct parent \u2192 exits non-zero with a redundant with hierarchy error message; no LINK event written.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system behavior where the system detects and rejects redundant hierarchical relationships by exiting non-zero and not writing LINK events"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "SC8: ticket link task-A story-X blocks|depends_on (or the reverse) where story-X is task-A's direct parent \u2192 exits non-zero with a redundant with hierarchy error message; no LINK event written.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes the durable system behavior of detecting and handling redundant hierarchy relationships by exiting non-zero and suppressing LINK events"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "SC9: Attempting to create a circular or self-referential dependency at the redirected level (epic-to-epic or story-to-story, including self-loops where source and target resolve to the same ticket) \u2192 exits non-zero with a clear error; no LINK event written.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 5,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system behavior (error handling for circular dependencies) that persists once implemented, phrased as ongoing system capability"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "SC10: Tickets with no parent_id (orphan tickets) \u2192 link written as-is; no redirect or error.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system behavior for how orphan tickets are handled, phrased as ongoing functionality rather than a one-time migration task"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "SC11: If .cache.json is missing for any ticket encountered during hierarchy resolution, the operation fails with an explicit error rather than silently treating the ticket as an orphan.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 5,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system behavior (explicit error handling) that will persist as long as the code exists, not a one-time migration task"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "SC12: ticket_type values in .cache.json are compared case-insensitively during cycle detection scoping (handles \"epic\" and \"Epic\" variants).",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system behavior (case-insensitive comparison) that will remain true after implementation and ongoing"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "SC13: Hierarchy resolution reads at most 4 .cache.json files per ticket link call (at most 2 per ticket end, at most 2 hops up). Performance validated by a benchmark test running ticket link against a synthetic ticket tree of 1,000 tickets completing in under 5 seconds on a developer workstation.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable performance constraint and system behavior that persists after implementation, with validation confirming the property holds"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "SC14: End-to-end dep-graph validation \u2014 given a synthetic ticket tree (1 epic, 2 stories, 2 tasks per story), running ticket link task-A task-B depends_on where task-A and task-B are under different stories of the same epic must produce: (a) ticket show story-X lists story-X to story-Y as a dependency in its deps output, and (b) ticket show task-A does NOT list task-A to task-B in its deps output. Both assertions verified by a sprint acceptance test run within the session.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "transitional",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a one-time acceptance test verification task to validate system behavior rather than an ongoing durable property"
      },
      "user_decision": "accept",
      "post_migration_section": "CC"
    }
  ]
